<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="206" project="customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Remediate 32 recipe-contract violations in scripts/provisioning-prereqs/prereqs.yaml (SESSION 12 exit-1 contract was written but never applied beyond PRQ-E-14)</title>
    <phase>Post-Live-Fire remediation — prereqs manifest correctness</phase>
    <gate>startable</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Modifies the manifest that gates every customer provisioning run (Step 0.5). A silent-PASS false positive on any recipe here is the exact failure mode the manifest exists to catch (F16/F19/F20/T108/F14 root causes). Each recipe fix requires understanding what "success" looks like for that specific check + adding an appropriate `exit 1` guard.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Mechanical per-recipe: convert `az command` to `result=$(az command); [ -n "$result" ] || exit 1` or similar with the specific assertion the `expect:` field describes. No architectural judgment beyond honoring the SKILL Step 0.5b author contract.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>xhigh</effort>
    <effort-reason>32 recipes across 27 prereqs. Each requires reading the recipe, understanding its assertion, authoring the exit-1 guard, verifying the guard behaves correctly (exits on failure, exits 0 on success). Non-trivial testing per recipe. Brownfield analysis of what each `az` / `pac` call actually returns on success vs failure. **Amended 2026-08-27 (PRQ-10)**: added 8-recipe assertion-recompute scope (E-06 per-service role map, E-11 AND-condition Sender+Receiver, S-03 failed=0 loop, C-01 numeric limit>current, C-02 3-pin iteration, C-04 numeric used<limit, C-06 numeric >=25600000, plus any others surfaced in re-audit). Assertion RECOMPUTE is a heavier lift than exit-1-wrapper — several recipes required per-service data maps, bash-4 associative arrays, jq assertions, or loop restructures. Revised estimate: 8-12h (was 4-6h).</effort-reason>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <deps>199</deps>
    <tags>provisioning, prereqs-manifest, silent-fail-remediation, skill-directive, recipe-hardening</tags>
    <estimated-effort>8-12h (careful per-recipe work; cannot batch mechanically; assertion-recompute scope adds ~4h over the exit-1-only estimate)</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Every prereq in `scripts/provisioning-prereqs/prereqs.yaml` EXCEPT PRQ-E-14 violates the SKILL Step 0.5b recipe-author contract: recipes MUST explicitly `exit 1` on any internal failure condition, not rely on `az`/`pac` empty-output-implies-fail. The audit surfaced 32 specific violations. Full per-recipe defect list + proposed fix pattern is in `projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/notes/prereqs-yaml-audit-2026-08-27.md` § Class B, sourced from workflow `wf_75aa08a8-13e` transcript.

The most consequential violations (each silently PASSES on the exact defect the prereq exists to catch):
- PRQ-C-02 — OpenAI model lifecycle status → silent PASS on Deprecated (the EXACT SESSION 12 regression that motivated the contract)
- PRQ-E-06 — L2 UAMI RBAC on source Azure services → silent PASS on absent role assignments (F19/F20 root cause)
- PRQ-E-09 — KV canonical secret catalog presence → silent PASS on partial-seeding (F16 root cause)
- PRQ-E-12 — Service Bus queue requiresSession + requiresDuplicateDetection → silent PASS on wrong settings (T108 recreate-ceremony)
- PRQ-C-06 — Dataverse maxuploadfilesize ≥25MB → silent PASS on default 5MB (F14 SpaarkeMaster import fail)
- PRQ-C-07 — uses PowerShell `Select-String` inside `bash -c` wrapper → silently emits "command not found" every iteration; loop exits 0 regardless of app presence

Apply the exit-1 guard pattern to every recipe. Verify each via manual invocation on a canary state (broken + fixed).</prompt>

  <role>Main-session operator (skill-directive hot-path — `scripts/provisioning-prereqs/prereqs.yaml` is not under `.claude/` but the file governs skill Step 0.5 behavior and is treated as skill-adjacent).</role>

  <goal>Every prereq in prereqs.yaml `check_recipe.cli` explicitly `exit 1` on any failure condition its `expect:` field describes. The SESSION 14 `validate.ps1` forcing function continues to PASS. A companion smoke test proves that a synthesized failure state (e.g., a fake absent role assignment) triggers `exit 1` on the affected recipe.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      SESSION 12 (2026-08-26 authoring of prereqs.yaml v3.3) rewrote SKILL Step 0.5b to reject the empty-output-implies-fail pattern. The stated reason: PRQ-C-02 (OpenAI model catalog check) silently passed when westus2 returned zero models, because the classifier defaulted to non-empty output = pass and fell through to a generic "output could be anything" branch. The FIX was to make recipes exit-code-first: recipe MUST explicitly `exit 1`.

      SESSION 14 (2026-08-27) discovered — via the first-live Step 0.5 iteration — that ONLY PRQ-E-14 was updated to honor the new contract. Every other recipe still uses empty-output-implies-fail or relies on `az`'s undocumented HTTP-status-to-exit mapping. This means Step 0.5 will iterate cleanly (parseability fixed by task 199), report PASS on almost everything, and hand back a false green signal to the operator.

      This task is the systematic sweep to actually implement what SESSION 12 declared.

      **PRQ-10 amendment (2026-08-27)**: Task originally spec'd as "add exit-1 guard" — the SESSION 15 pre-dispatch audit surfaced that 8 of the recipes require full assertion-RECOMPUTE (not just wrapper) because their `expect:` field describes a SPECIFIC condition (numeric threshold, per-service role map, AND-condition, multi-pin iteration) that the current recipe does not test. A naive exit-1-on-empty wrapper would still silent-PASS the exact defect the prereq exists to catch. See notes/pre-dispatch-audit-punchlist-2026-08-27.md § PRQ-03, PRQ-10, PRQ-12 for the full analysis and the SESSION 12 mistake-at-one-meta-level-up framing. Acceptance criterion 6 enumerates the 8 recipes + the 12 additional SESSION 14 empty-output sweep recipes.

      **Non-goal**: this task does NOT fix placeholder-substitution defects (see task 207). Placeholder tokens like `{l2UamiPrincipalId}` will remain as literals in recipes until task 207 lands. The exit-1 guards authored here will help by making the false-fail loud rather than silent, but the eventual fix requires both classes remediated.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="target">scripts/provisioning-prereqs/prereqs.yaml</file>
      <file role="skill-contract">.claude/skills/provision-environment/SKILL.md § Step 0.5b</file>
      <file role="audit-source">projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/notes/prereqs-yaml-audit-2026-08-27.md</file>
      <file role="forcing-function">scripts/provisioning-prereqs/validate.ps1</file>
      <file role="reference-implementation">PRQ-E-14 recipe in prereqs.yaml (the ONE prereq that honors the contract)</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="199" status="completed">Task 199 SESSION 14 established the parseable manifest baseline + forcing function. Task 206 sweeps recipes on top of that baseline.</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="skill-Step-0.5b">Recipe MUST explicitly `exit 1` on any failure condition it detects internally. Silent empty output no longer implicitly passes.</constraint>
    <constraint source="validate.ps1-forcing-function">Every edit MUST leave the manifest parseable AND the forcing function passing. Run `pwsh -File scripts/provisioning-prereqs/validate.ps1` after each recipe edit.</constraint>
    <constraint source="check_recipe.expect-field">Each recipe's `expect:` field describes what success looks like. The exit-1 guard MUST assert against that expect condition, not just non-empty output.</constraint>
    <constraint source="reference-pattern">PRQ-E-14 (currently the only compliant recipe) is the reference implementation. Use its shape as the template.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion>Every recipe in `scripts/provisioning-prereqs/prereqs.yaml check_recipe.cli` **computes the specific assertion its `expect:` field describes and exits 1 with an actionable diagnostic on failure** — NOT merely wraps the existing az/pac output with a naive non-empty-implies-pass guard. The bar is: recipe would exit 1 when the SPECIFIC condition the prereq exists to catch is present, exit 0 only when the exact assertion succeeds.</criterion>
    <criterion>PRQ-C-07 uses bash-native commands (grep -q, [ -n "$var" ], etc.) — NO PowerShell cmdlets under bash -c wrapper.</criterion>
    <criterion>Running `pwsh -File scripts/provisioning-prereqs/validate.ps1` PASSES (exit 0) after all edits.</criterion>
    <criterion>Smoke test: pick 3 recipes, synthesize a failing state (mock env var, mock az output, etc.), verify each recipe now exits 1 loudly with actionable message.</criterion>
    <criterion>Companion PR description enumerates each recipe modified + the specific assertion added.</criterion>
    <criterion source="PRQ-10 amendment 2026-08-27">The following 8 recipes require full assertion-RECOMPUTE (not just exit-1 wrapper). Each recipe's fix commit / diff MUST include a comment linking to its assertion class:
      - **PRQ-E-06** — per-service required role map inline (openai/docintel=Cognitive Services User, search=Search Service Contributor, servicebus=Azure Service Bus Data Owner, storage=Storage Account Contributor, redis=Redis Cache Contributor); assert EACH service has EXACT expected role
      - **PRQ-E-11** — AND-condition assertion for both Azure Service Bus Data Sender AND Azure Service Bus Data Receiver via separate grep checks (prior OR query silent-passed on single-role)
      - **PRQ-S-03** — `failed=0` flag loop pattern (prior loop always exited 0 on partial-registration)
      - **PRQ-C-01** — numeric `limit > current` assertion via jq for every returned frontier tier entry (fresh-sub limit=0 silent-PASSes without this)
      - **PRQ-C-02** — iterate 3 explicit pins (mirror PRQ-E-14); drop nonsense {pinnedVer} single-value placeholder; per-pin GenerallyAvailable/Legacy assertion
      - **PRQ-C-04** — numeric `used &lt; limit` assertion (was: `pac admin quota` — PRQ-07 also swaps to az rest against BAP API)
      - **PRQ-C-06** — numeric `>= 25600000` assertion (default 5MB silent-PASSes without this)
      - **12 additional recipes from the SESSION 14 empty-output-implies-fail sweep** (T-03, T-04, T-05, T-06, T-07, S-04, E-03, E-04, E-05, E-09, E-10, C-05) also touched in the same sweep. C-05 was subsequently marked server-side-only (PRQ-02).
    See notes/pre-dispatch-audit-punchlist-2026-08-27.md § PRQ-03, PRQ-10, PRQ-12 for the full analysis.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>
</task>
